  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\residue.theorem]\nTheorem:\ngiven:\n. a, b is \\real\n. gamma is \\(closed)::complex.path:on{a, b}\n. f is \\function:on{\\complex.numbers}:to{\\complex.numbers}\n. z0 is \\complex\nthen:\n. exists: I is \\complex\n  suchThat: I = \\contour.integral:of{f}:along{gamma}\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Residue Theorem\"\n. description: \"The contour integral of a meromorphic function equals $2\\pi i$\n                times the sum of the residues enclosed by the contour.\"\nId: \"3069a9a0-50d1-4424-b9e6-783a50b65cb5\"",
